course: dictionary
lesson: 3040
title: Earplug: a small thing with a big job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An earplug is a noun, a naming word for a thing. The word is made of two smaller words, ear and plug. A plug fills a gap, so an earplug fills the inside of your ear. Try putting «an earplug» or «a pair of earplugs» into a sentence, and you can see it is a thing you can hold and wear.
explain: Look at the words around it to work out the meaning. «Loud gigs need earplugs» tells you earplugs are for loud places. «Very loud sound for a long time damages the tiny hairs in your ears» tells you why people wear them: to protect their hearing.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Many fans wear earplugs» becomes «many fans wear a small soft piece of foam in their ears to keep out noise», and it still makes sense. That is a good sign you have the right meaning.
fact: An earplug is a noun: a thing you can hold, wear and put in your ear.
fact: An earplug is a small soft piece of foam, wax or rubber.
fact: People put earplugs in their ears to keep out noise or water.
fact: «Wear earplugs» and «put in earplugs» are phrases you can use with this word.
fact: The plural is earplugs, and «a pair of earplugs» means two of them, one for each ear.
exercise: «Many fans wear earplugs at big festivals.» What is an earplug? | *A small soft piece of foam, wax or rubber you put in your ear | A kind of hat for cold weather | A bright light you hold at a concert | A loud drum on stage
exercise: «Very loud sound for a long time damages the tiny hairs in your ears, so people wear earplugs.» Why do people wear earplugs here? | To make their hair look tidy | *To keep out loud sound and protect their hearing | To listen to music faster | To swim in deep water
exercise: «Cinemas can be very loud; covering your ears or using earplugs is fine.» Find and copy one word that is a noun for a thing you can put in your ears. | covering | cinemas | loud | *earplugs
test: Ella says an earplug is a kind of music. What is the true meaning? | A type of loud drum | A ticket for a concert | A loud speaker on stage | *A small soft piece of foam, wax or rubber you put in your ear
test: «Musicians' earplugs make sound quieter but still clear.» What does this sentence tell you about musicians' earplugs? | They make everything silent | They are only for children | *They make sound quieter but still clear | They stop musicians from playing
exam: Jayden asks, «Is an earplug a noun?» What is the answer? | No, it is a verb for listening | *Yes, it is a thing you can wear in your ear | No, it is a feeling of sadness | Yes, it is a place where loud music is played
